tion_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":["AP-3","AP-14"],"id":"AX-5","kind":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: `status(composite)=meet(status(parts))`; no evidence defaults to blocked, and later stages may lower but not raise authority without a new derivation.","principles":["P-2","P-6","P-15","P-19"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The checklist only has pass and fail; the system scores trust on several separate measures at once.","maps":[{"analogy":"the flight is grounded by its one failing check","doctrine":"the combined result is only as trusted as its weakest part"},{"analogy":"a blank checklist item counts as not done","doctrine":"missing evidence counts as blocked"}],"text":"A plane does not take off because most of the pre-flight checklist passed. One required check left blank keeps it at the gate."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A status board marks a combined result green because no part reported a failure, counting a check that never ran as a pass.","does_not_prove":"A result that is not blocked has only passed the checks that ran; staying blocked by default says nothing about whether the result is correct.","enforced_in_component_ids":["batch12_release_claim_language_gate","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","self_ignorance_coverage_ledger"],"example":{"component_ids":["batch12_release_claim_language_gate"],"text":"The release wording gate reads the system's own public text and stops the export when it finds overclaiming wording, so a later packaging step cannot make a stronger claim than the checks beneath it support."},"governs":"What status missing evidence gets, and in which direction a status may change between stages.","plain":"Something built from parts is only as trusted as its weakest required part. A part with no evidence counts as blocked, and a later step can lower trust but never quietly raise it.","potential_misread":"That enough passing parts can outweigh a blocked one, when the weakest required part sets the status of the whole.","refuses":"Passing something by default when no check ran.","requires":"The lowest of the parts' statuses as the combined status, blocked for any part without evidence, and a new check before any stage raises a status.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A missing check is treated as a reason to stop, so a release that finds private material or overclaiming wording stops instead of shipping."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-5","statement":"Formal clause: `status(composite)=meet(status(parts))`; no evidence defaults to\nblocked, and later stages may lower but not raise authority without a new\nderivation.\n\nLineage: lattice information flow, fail-safe defaults, monotone dataflow.\n\nRoute: recorded as strongly witnessed by the Crown Jewel harness,\n`release_export`, `organ_evidence_classes.json::fail_closed_no_default`, and\nthe private-state and secret-exclusion scans. The release tests block an\nexport that would leak a result record's body or use overclaiming language.\n\nAnti-axiom: a part with no evidence passes silently by default.","statement_sha256":"1e1dac1ad3540d59a0bbe4e12ef4cf3668fcc05ec842bd27f9f6f7aa2b22f3d1","title":"Fail-closed monotone lattice","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}